KNOWNBUG: C++20 libstdc++ pair's requires-clause + explicit(bool)
converting constructor pair(U1&&, U2&&) is instantiated WITHOUT a body
(constexpr/macro-flagged symbol, nil value, never queued deferred);
symex havocs the call, so both members are garbage.  --cpp17 works
(enable_if-based pair).  Root blocker for cpp20_map_basic
(_M_get_insert_unique_pos's _Res(__y, 0)).  Flip to CORE when fixed.

PROGRESS 2026-07-17: the constraint side is fixed -- requires-clause
call atoms (_S_constructible<...>()) are now constant-folded during
candidate filtering, so overload resolution no longer keeps unviable
candidates whose bodies then hard-fail ("invalid implicit conversion
from 'signed int' to 'struct nodet *'").  RESIDUAL: the correctly
selected converting constructor's body STILL fails its system-header-
lenient conversion (silently; symbol left nil) and the pair members
remain nondet.  Next step: surface that conversion error (disable the
syshdr guard for this symbol under a debugger) and fix the body-side
defect -- likely in the explicit(bool) handling or the mem-initializer
forwarding (first(std::forward<_U1>(__x))).
